fix:
Introduce size bounds and a mechanism to drain excess buffers back to a global thread-safe allocator or pool.
```rust
const MAX_LOCAL_POOL_SIZE: usize = 16;

pub fn free_block(block: Vec<u8>) {
    LOCAL_BLOCK_POOL.with(|pool| {
        let mut pool = pool.borrow_mut();
        if pool.len() < MAX_LOCAL_POOL_SIZE {
            pool.push(block);
        } // Otherwise, drop the block and let the global allocator reclaim it.
    })
}
```
